From: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tplink-safeloader: give the file system the whole rest of the
 firmware partition

The size of the file-system partition is what is left of the firmware
partition after the kernel, but the offset of the firmware partition in
the flash was taken off as well. The root file system was refused that
many bytes before the partition was full: 128 KiB on most layouts, and
384 KiB where the firmware starts at 0x60000.

Signed-off-by: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
---
 src/tplink-safeloader.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/tplink-safeloader.c
+++ b/src/tplink-safeloader.c
@@ -3940,7 +3940,8 @@
 		if (!sysupgrade)
 			file_system_partition->base = ALIGN(firmware_partition->base + kernel.st_size, 0x10000);
 
-		file_system_partition->size = firmware_partition->size - file_system_partition->base;
+		file_system_partition->size = firmware_partition->base + firmware_partition->size -
+					      file_system_partition->base;
 
 		os_image_partition->name = info->partition_names.os_image;
 
